From: DevOs <devos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] proxy: support the DevOS desktop with the GSettings resolver

DevOs provides a native editor for the same per-user GSettings proxy schema.
Enable that resolver without advertising the desktop as GNOME to other apps.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [DevOs integration]
---
 proxy/gnome/gproxyresolvergnome.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/proxy/gnome/gproxyresolvergnome.c b/proxy/gnome/gproxyresolvergnome.c
--- a/proxy/gnome/gproxyresolvergnome.c
+++ b/proxy/gnome/gproxyresolvergnome.c
@@ -359,7 +359,8 @@ g_proxy_resolver_gnome_is_supported (GProxyResolver *object)
    * pretend to be GNOME and want to use our proxy settings will list
    * themselves alongside GNOME. That's fine; they'll get our proxy settings.
    */
-  return strstr (desktops, "GNOME") != NULL;
+  return strstr (desktops, "GNOME") != NULL ||
+         strstr (desktops, "DevOS") != NULL;
 }
 
